{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory spans 62 turns over a prolonged post-discharge episode. All seven responsibility-chain (RC) items are met without serious or minor error. Four high-order points are each completed with active model actions: HO1 (reconciling incomplete handoff and pending surgery status), HO2 (correcting caregiver misconceptions about medicines dissolving stones and insulin misunderstanding), HO3 (dynamically reprioritizing around poor intake, missed insulin, and ongoing biliary risk), and HO4 (bounded closure distinguishing emergency-blocking from acceptable residual risks). No important non-chain defect exists. The closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid. With ≥2 HO points completed, the maximum grade 5 Perfect is reached.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_01297",
        "explanation": "Final summary confirms understanding of bounded plan, emergency thresholds, and pending outpatient follow-up.",
        "quote": "按你现在反馈，暂时算相对平稳"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The model closes with a clear, structured plan differentiating emergency scenarios from outpatient follow-up, medication monitoring, and pending surgical decision, and obtains caregiver receipt.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
